1,Shoo-Minda-Nye language,https://grokipedia.com/page/shoo_minda_nye_language,"Shoo-Minda-Nye is a Jukunoid language of the Benue-Congo branch within the Niger-Congo family, spoken primarily in Taraba State, Nigeria, by communities in areas such as Karim Lamido Local Government Area.",Shoo-Minda-Nye,Niger-Congo
2,Shoo-Minda-Nye Language (BCV)... | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/language/bcv/,"Shoo-Minda-Nye is a stable indigenous language of Nigeria. It belongs to the Niger-Congo language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Shoo-Minda-Nye,Niger-Congo
